# The quadgram table is a derived file, and QuadgramTableReproducibilityTest compares it to what
# the corpus regenerates: Files.readString on one side, a string built in memory on the other, and
# an exact comparison between them. Checked out with CRLF, the two differ by a carriage return per
# line and the build stops for a reason that has nothing to do with the corpus.
#
# data/corpus/MANIFEST.md says the line endings were normalised to LF "so the table generates
# identically on every platform". Without this file that was true of what is committed and false
# of what a Windows runner checks out.
* text=auto eol=lf
